<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Wired at step P4 of docs/ios-appstore-release.md (paid team, 2026-10-06). Both capabilities ship
  DORMANT and switch on from the server, with no new binary:
  - Universal links answer only once eno.vn serves /.well-known/apple-app-site-association, which
    needs APPLE_TEAM_ID in eno-vn.env (step P7). Until then iOS finds no association and links
    keep opening Safari.
  - aps-environment lets native push work once APNs is configured and NEXT_PUBLIC_NATIVE_PUSH_IOS=1
    is set (step P8). Xcode re-signs it as `production` when the archive is exported for App Store
    Connect.
  ⛔ applinks:eno.vn AND NOTHING ELSE (owner, 2026-10-06: "ship both with eno.vn"). The app renders
  the licensed marketplace and its company is the App Store seller, so eno.vn is the domain that
  vouches for it. NEVER an eno.forum host: the forum carries the services the licensed company may
  not offer, and a claimed forum link would open this app instead of the browser. A claim in a
  submitted binary can only be withdrawn by another submission; scripts/ios-release.sh refuses any
  other set. www.eno.vn 308s to the apex for every path, the association file included, so it could
  never be listed anyway.
  No Sign in with Apple: decision D2 = b (Google is hidden in the iOS app instead).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:eno.vn</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
